Applied by tools/build_hactool.py to SciresM/hactool (ISC) at 1d64a83450e025622f3468c28fc4164dad2c5ef6, after
portable.patch; ours. Two memory errors AddressSanitizer finds in the update merge of tools/extract.py:

- nca.c, nca_process_bktr_section: the relocation and subsection buckets are spread in place from a 0x4000-byte stride
  to one 20 (relocation) or 16 (subsection) bytes longer, so each destination overlaps its source. memcpy on
  overlapping ranges is undefined. It happens to work where memcpy is memmove (x86-64 glibc, macOS, Windows); aarch64
  glibc's memcpy corrupts the buckets and the merge crashes with SIGSEGV. memmove is defined for the overlap.
- extkeys.c, get_kv: a key line longer than the 1024-byte line buffer (a Lockpick prod.keys's eticket_rsa_keypair has
  1078 characters) is read without its newline, and trimming its trailing whitespace wrote one byte past the buffer.
  Such a line now ends at its terminator; its remaining characters come as the next line, which is no valid
  `name = value` line and is skipped as before.

